  "findings": [
    "HIA1 fills all six literal HidaPropsAlt fields from the completed endpoints on the given IsJ. It preserves the point field rank antecedent, the exact end1/end2 aliases, conditional continuity, V0ok only where originally guarded, and the nonvacuous pt argument in the top-ideal branch.",
    "HIA2 constructs actual empty-Q Hecke data and the one IsJ over the supplied coefficient ring, then attaches HidaPropsAlt and full HasAut from the same LevelAlt family. IsCoef and the original bz, geo and tame-local foundations are explicitly matched. All original positive-rank, noMu, Large, universal-ring and weight-object quantifiers are retained.",
    "HIA3 proves the residual cyclotomic condition on the actual level quotient from noMu. Its general ModularAlt/ModUAlt implication has exactly the original CohP, LocCFTAll, PfromAut and HidaUAlt antecedents; P3core is never inferred from the selected one-point proof.",
    "HIA4 matches all six original JSP11 support suppliers on the same normalized point, chosen full-block Kap and actual Taylor-Wiles realization: CIP normalization; CAP Phi-finiteness and ArPl in their required order; CCH choice and N4 preservation; full pro-ell kernel condition; CFO first-order and CCH zero obstruction constants; SCI13 selected Raw. The same ideal and all original P1core tests are retained. It uses no arbitrary-chain PfromAut.",
    "HIA5 reproduces the actual glueN scope in human form. At each eligible finite place one of the excluded-place windows applies. Its strict half-width rules out a q-ratio, giving toral unlinked support; the prior single center from HAW6 then works at every eligible place. This does not presume equal input centers or add continuity to AutCsd0.",
    "HIA6 fixes the tower and iota before QX4 coefficient threshold, both actual Links and later B/Lambda. ITA/HLM/Hida constructions require no new outer coefficient extension, while normalization/support extensions lie inside the later point quantifier. Both ideals carry all seven required fields in their own original rings; the common threshold precedes every Space. The actual QX10/YX2 consumers retain their independent background inputs. Distinct auxiliary rational primes give distinct underlying finite places and justify HIA5 when the consumer supplies the same twisted representation.",
    "The full original selected COUNT_II_SUPPORT contract is therefore discharged, including both Links, same-J properties, prime 3, fixed iota, full determinant/pro-ell conditions, CohP/LocCFT and the prior common threshold. This does not discharge the remaining case, quantitative or common-family producers or general arbitrary-chain P3core."
  ],
